## [6.11.0] — 2026-09-25 — Daraja STK Push + Lipa na M-PESA C2B (protocol-first)

### Added

- **Daraja STK Push (Lipa na M-PESA) live end-to-end** — Safaricom Daraja edges ship
  (ADR-012 supersedes the ADR-004 Phase-2 deferral):
  - `stk-push` (JWT initiate edge) + `lipa-na-mpesa-callback` (public Safaricom
    callback edge), both type-checked by `npm run check:functions` (`deno check`).
    *(Correction: at v6.11.0 this gate existed as an npm script only — it was NOT
    wired into CI until v6.12.0. See v6.12.0.)*
  - `_shared/daraja/protocol.ts` — the single source of truth: phone→254 normalization,
    KES range enforcement (1–150,000 whole shillings), AccountReference/TransactionDesc
    caps, Safaricom timestamp + STK password builders, payload builder, initiate/callback
    parsers, `buildCallbackVerdict`. 32 vitest tests cover it.
  - Fail-closed at the boundary: missing `DARAJA_*` env → `503 DARAJA_NOT_CONFIGURED`;
    forged/amount-mismatched callback → `IGNORED` verdict (audit row written, **money
    never written**); every callback (PAID/FAILED/IGNORED) lands in `daftari_stk_callbacks`.

### Changed

- **`daftari_transactions.source` now consumes the reserved `'daraja'` slot** — the
  income for a PAID STK request is written through the existing mirror path, typed as
  `income` with `local_id` from the request.
- `.env.example` documents the server-only `DARAJA_*` block (sandbox first) + how to
  flip `DARAJA_ENV` to production after the drill (operator-guide §2.1, ADR-012).
- `source` filter/uses in the app treat `daraja` as a first-class income source.

### Operator action

- Add the 8 `DARAJA_*` secrets to **Supabase Functions → Secrets** (never Vercel, never
  `VITE_*`). Config keys from the Safaricom Daraja portal (sandbox). See the
  `docs/runbook/daraja-stk-push.md` STK-Push drill before pointing at production.

## [6.10.0] — 2026-09-24 (Catalog Cost Price + Barcode + Services)

### Added
- **Product catalog domain** (`src/lib/catalog.ts`): pure, tested authority for cost-price parsing
  (fail-closed via `parseKESInput`, empty = unknown cost, never coerced garbage), barcode
  normalization + uniqueness (`findBarcodeConflict`, whitespace-insensitive, self-edit aware),
  per-unit margin (`computeProductMargin` via `kesSubtract`/`kesPercent`), and the
  product-vs-service distinction (`isService`) with save-time stock clearing
  (`normalizeProductForSave`). New money helper `kesPercent` inside `src/lib/money.ts` keeps all
  margin math inside the sanctioned ADR-007 module.
- **Catalog UI** (`ProductCatalogScreen`): cost price + barcode fields on add and edit (pencil),
  price-comparison warning when cost exceeds selling price, duplicate-barcode rejection, per-card
  margin line (only when a cost is actually set) and barcode chip, and a "Mark as Service" switch
  that hides stock fields and drops stock bookkeeping on save.
- **Sale-path wiring**: `RecordSale` quick-add and single-product `PosScreen` checkout now snapshot
  `product_id` + `cost_price` into the transaction, so quick sales stop starving profitability;
  blended multi-product carts intentionally record no product attribution. Service lines never
  decrement stock in either path, and a service-only POS checkout performs no no-op stock write.
- **Honest profitability** (`ProductProfitabilityScreen`): products whose sales have no known cost
  now render "no cost set" instead of a false revenue-as-profit figure, with a summary warning that
  total margin may be overstated until cost prices are entered.
- New tests: catalog domain (17), ProductCatalogScreen (7), POS snapshot/service tests (3),
  RecordSale snapshot/service tests (2). i18n 317/317 in use (both locales).
- Sprint doc: `docs/changelog/sprint-v6-10-0-catalog-cost-barcode-services.md`.

### Fixed
- **Midnight-timezone flake in tests**: `DashboardScreen.test.tsx` and `DailyClose.test.tsx`
  fixtures used UTC `new Date().toISOString()` while the screens filter by Nairobi date — they
  dropped transactions between 00:00–03:00 EAT. Fixtures now build `recorded_at` from the Nairobi
  day via `vi.hoisted`, so the suite is green at any hour.

### Engineering
- Catalog rules enforced at the single boundary (`src/lib/catalog.ts`) shared by catalog screen,
  POS, and quick-add — the UI cannot drift from the sale path.
- Unknown cost is treated as *unknown*, never zero: margin figures and profitability summaries
  only surface when `cost_price` is present on at least one sale.
- No Dexie schema change (`products` remains JSONB on the business row); database VERSION stays 7.
- Version 6.10.0 in `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and `APP.VERSION`.

## [6.9.0] — 2026-09-23 (Hybrid Niches + Receiving Accounts + CEO Dashboard + Scale)

### Added
- **Hybrid multi-niche module**: `daftari_businesses` gains `categories`, `subcategories`,
  `receiving_accounts` (jsonb, migration `20260923000000`, pushed live). End-to-end model support
  (`db.ts`, `store.ts`, `businessId.ts`), pull/realtime normalization of the JSONB columns, and a
  `businessCategories.ts` aggregation layer (`resolveActiveCategories`, `resolveActivePairs`,
  `aggregateIncomeCategories`, `aggregateTemplateProducts`) wired into `RecordSale`
  and `ProductCatalogScreen`. Onboarding persists full category/subcategory arrays while keeping
  the primary category for backward compatibility.
- **Receiving-account contract** (`receivingAccount.ts`): per-method destination validation
  (M-Pesa/Airtel phone, pochi, till, paybill, bank; `cash`/`card_pos` exempt), fail-closed for
  account-requiring methods. New onboarding **Step 7** collects confirmations before the
  push-permission step; `PaymentMethodsScreen` and `BusinessProfileScreen` show/edit them.
- **Admin CEO dashboard**: migrations `20260923000001` (admin tables, `is_admin()`
  security-definer, `admin_metrics()` RPC, presence + payment-confirmation ledgers) and
  `20260923000003` (paged `admin_businesses()` + `record_presence()`) — pushed live. Client is
  **server-authoritative** and fail-closed (`src/lib/admin.ts`): role resolved from `is_admin()`
  in `App.tsx`, dashboard reads `admin_metrics()` (revenue, profit, online-now, 7d chart), paged
  business list, presence heartbeat `usePresenceHeartbeat`, Settings admin row gated on role.
- **Scale hardening**: migration `20260923000002` (indexes + realtime publication self-heal);
  `syncAll.ts` push now batches (50/chunk, concurrency 4) with per-row fallback, and pull uses
  prefetch + `bulkPut` with newest-wins (was row-by-row).
- New tests: hybrid categories (18), receiving accounts (8), AdminScreen server gate + paging (4;
  existing 2 rewritten), syncAll batched paths (16). i18n 306/306 in use (both locales).
- Sprint doc: `docs/changelog/sprint-v6-9-0-hybrid-niches-trust-admin.md`.

### Fixed
- **Sync correctness**: `repository.updateBusiness` now marks the row `synced: 0`, so business
  edits re-upload instead of silently staying local forever.
- **Settings gate**: payment-methods row un-gated from the client `VITE_ADMIN_USER_ID` env flag —
  admin authority now lives only on the server (`daftari_admin_users`).
- **Flaky test**: `monitoring.test.ts` dynamic imports given a 15s timeout under full-suite load.

### Engineering
- Money law held end-to-end in the admin dashboard: server-aggregated KES is only ever *displayed*
  via `formatKES(toKES(...))`, never re-arithmetized client-side.
- Fail-closed guarantees: non-admin calls to `admin_metrics()` / `admin_businesses()` raise
  `FORBIDDEN: admin only` server-side; client resolves any error to "not admin".
- Daraja STK/C2B remains deferred; the trust engine ships its foundation as the
  receiving-account contract + `daftari_payment_confirmations` ledger (schema only).
- Admin seeding (owner must run in Supabase SQL editor):
  `insert into public.daftari_admin_users (user_id) values ('<owner-auth-uid>');`
- Version 6.9.0 in `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and `APP.VERSION`.

## [6.8.0] — 2026-09-22 (Subscription & Billing)

### Added
- **Subscription infrastructure**: `daftari_subscriptions` table + `daftari_subscription_requests`
  table (migrations `20260922000000`/`20260922000001`) with RLS policies, an idempotent
  security-definer signup trigger that seeds a 30-day trial, and a `user_subscription` view
  created with `security_invoker = true` so RLS is never bypassed (PG15+).
- **Tier model** (`msingi` / `biashara` / `biashara_plus`), `TIER_FEATURES` entitlement map, and the
  fail-closed access layer `src/lib/subscription.ts` (only a provably active subscription — or an
  in-window trial — unlocks premium features; an unloadable row is never treated as full access).
- **`useSubscription` hook**: fetches live from the view, keeps a validated localStorage cache,
  fails closed on malformed/no rows, and never flashes premium content while loading.
- **`FeatureGate` + `UpgradeScreen`**: locked cards route to an M-Pesa purchase sheet that submits a
  pending `subscription_request` (tier + amount), and five premium surfaces are now gated:
  monthly report, suppliers, purchase orders, POS mode, customer tracking.
- **Trial countdown banner** in the app shell (`≤7 days` → upgrade CTA) and a subscription
  summary card in Settings (tier, status, price).
- **`requireReauth()`** guard (re-authenticate before destructive actions) — fails closed on any
  missing/expired session; the app currently has no account-deletion caller, so it ships as tested
  infrastructure awaiting a real boundary.
- **Load test**: `scripts/load-test.js` (k6: static shell GET, ramp 20→50→100, p(95)<2s, <5%
  errors) and the `npm run test:load` script.
- New tests: subscription access logic (23), useSubscription fail-closed paths (10), FeatureGate
  gating (5), UpgradeScreen submit flow (6), TrialCountdownBanner (5), requireReauth (5).
- **i18n**: 35 new keys in both `sw.json` and `en.json` (290 each, zero unused); `check-i18n.ts`
  now registers UpgradeScreen + SettingsScreen as dynamic-key sites.

### Engineering
- Money law held: all plan pricing is whole-KES display constants (0/299/799) rendered via
  `formatKES(toKES(...))` — no raw arithmetic outside `src/lib/money.ts`.
- Version 6.8.0 in `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, and `APP.VERSION`.

### Added
- **Animated niche marquee** on the landing screen, between the hero and the problem section,
  matching `public/daftari_niche_marquee_demo.html`: two rows of emoji pill chips scrolling
  continuously in opposite directions (Kiswahili forward `28s`, English reverse `22s`) beneath a
  combined bilingual header. Edges fade softly via a CSS mask, tracks are `width: max-content`
  inside an `overflow: hidden` wrapper so the page never scrolls horizontally, dark mode uses
  `dark:` Tailwind variants, and the keyframes live in a scoped `<style>` block. Content is
  Niche data, not UI strings — no new i18n keys.
- **Role-based reference docs**: `docs/user-guide.md` (user), `docs/operator-guide.md`
  (operator), `docs/programmer-guide.md` (programmer), cross-linked from `README.md` and from
  each other; `docs/deployment-runbook.md` documents the full release sequence.

### Fixed
- **AdminScreen** — resolved a JSX parse error (`))}`) that had masked the screen from the
  gates, imported the missing analytics helpers, and enforced a **fail-closed admin role guard**:
  `role !== 'admin'` returns "Not authorized" before any admin content renders. New test proves
  non-admins never see Revenue or Businesses sections, and admins do.
- **Store** — `role: 'user' | 'admin'` is now typed on `AppStore` with a `setRole` action and is
  **not persisted** (defaults to `'user'` on every boot, so the guard holds by default); restored
  the missing `language: 'sw'` in the initial state.
- **DB schema** — restored `products?: string` on the `Business` type (a WIP commit had replaced
  it with `categories`, breaking every `updateBusiness` product call site and failing
  typecheck across screens).
- **Onboarding** — restored the multi-select category state and the supabase import.
- **Payment Methods screen** — rebuilt against the real repository/`AppShell` API (requires
  `onBack`, loads/saves via `getBusiness`/`updateBusiness`), registered `'payment-methods'` in
  the `View` union, added the `manage_payment_methods` key to both language files.
- **Build wiring** — `APP.VERSION` synced to `6.7.0`; `openUrl` imports added in
  CustomerDetail and GrowthShare; `throttleWrite` rewritten with a generic async signature and
  explicit vitest imports; version assertion in the Settings test updated.

### Notes
- 415 tests green (42 files) across typecheck, lint, i18n parity, unit/component, and build.
- Tag `v6.7.0` re-pointed to the final green commit (it previously sat on an un-green commit).

