## [Unreleased] — 6.6.0 (Second Brain — DataBank Vault corridor)

### Added
- **Second Brain screen** (`SecondBrainScreen.tsx`, wired as a self-managed view in `AppShell` and
  reachable from Settings → Business Tools): capture a thought (with optional thread) into the
  DataBank vault, list the 20 most recent entries, and refresh. Stored via the vault's
  `PUT /vault/records` and `GET /vault/entries` — a typed, fail-closed browser client
  (`dataBankClient.ts`).
- **DataBank vault client** (`src/lib/dataBankClient.ts`): mirrors the DataBank Python
  `VaultClient` contract (`base_url` strip, `Authorization: Bearer`, `data.record` unwrap).
  Fail-closed rules enforced before any network call — blank token, blank URL, or blank text are
  refused as `Err` with a `VAULT_*` code; a 401/403 maps to `VAULT_AUTH_FAILED`, a network failure
  to `VAULT_UNREACHABLE`. This is the first raw-HTTP path in the app (everything else goes through
  supabase-js); it targets the tailnet-only vault, never a Supabase table.
- **Vault config section** (`VaultConfigSection.tsx` in Settings): lets the Owner set the vault
  server URL + token, persisted via the existing zustand persist layer alongside other on-device
  secrets. Empty config = vault fully disabled — the screen refuses to attempt any fetch.
- **Extended `AppErrorCode`** with `VAULT_UNREACHABLE`, `VAULT_AUTH_FAILED`, `VAULT_REFUSED`,
  `VAULT_NOT_CONFIGURED` so caller surfaces the real failure instead of a generic error.
- DataBank side (transport) landed in the DataBank repo as v0.6.2 (opt-in `--cors-origin`); the
  browser must be served over `http://localhost` (or the vault host must be https) because a secure
  page's mixed-content policy blocks plain-http tailnet hosts. 9 new tests: 7 client (mocked
  `fetch`) + 2 screen (fail-closed, refresh).

### Changed
- Version → 6.6.0 (`package.json`, `src/lib/constants.ts`).

## [Unreleased] — 6.5.0 (Install Hardening + Sync Wiring Seam)

### Added
- **Global install banner** (`InstallBanner.tsx`): persistent top-bar CTA on non-installed mobile
  browsers — an install button on Android/Chrome and Share→Add to Home Screen guidance on iOS
  Safari, with a one-tap dismiss. Auto-hidden once running installed (`display-mode: standalone` /
  `navigator.standalone === true`). 7 new jsdom tests.
- **Dead-button guarantee** in `usePWAInstall`: after any prompt outcome (accepted or dismissed) the
  deferred prompt is consumed and `canInstall` is cleared immediately — no more a no-op install
  button.
- **Visible sync config state**: `isSyncConfigured` exported from `src/lib/supabase.ts` (true only
  when both env vars are real, never the `localhost:0` fallback). Settings shows a colored dot +
  "Cloud sync is ready on this build" / "not configured".
- **Live sync verification** (`scripts/verify-sync-live.ts`, `npm run verify:sync:live`):
  real-network write→read→delete round-trip on the anon bearer path. Exit 0 = proven, 1 = not
  configured (the production gap), 2 = live failure.
- **Wiring runbook** (`docs/supabase-wiring.md`): the permanent sequence to set Vercel env (the real
  production compiler), apply migrations, rebuild, and verify the deployed bundle carries the real
  Supabase client.

### Fixed
- The silent gap where a production bundle could ship the `localhost:0` no-op client and still
  claim "syncs to cloud" — now surfaced in UI and caught by the verify script.
- `parseKESInput` accepted malformed money input (`1.5.5`→2, `1-2`→1, `15..5`→15) — garbage was
  silently written to the ledger as valid KES. Now the cleaned string must be well-formed
  (no `-`, at most one `.`, digits only) before conversion; anything else returns `null` so the
  caller surfaces an invalid entry. Forge task `adce53bbfa964dc8` (`f64acc5`).
- `check:i18n` hardcoded `DYNAMIC_KEYS` whitelist drifted — it flagged `yes_set_q1..3` as unused
  (they render via `t(q.key)`) and could silently ignore a dynamic key missing from the locales.
  The dynamic keys are now grepped from the real render sites (Onboarding options,
  Receipt literals) and a missing key **fails** the check instead of being noise.
  Forge task `bc7c1d3d0cd741a2` (`0af9d0f`).

### Changed
- Version → 6.5.0.

